# claude session-local state
# `.claude/*` and not `.claude/` — git never descends into an excluded
# DIRECTORY, so a `!` re-include underneath it can never match. Excluding the
# contents instead is what lets the skills below be tracked.
.claude/*
# ...except the skills, which are project assets the whole team shares.
# `.claude/skills/aura` is the design language the hub front door is built in;
# it has to travel with the repo or the next person rebuilds it by eye.
!.claude/skills/
.superpowers/

# vercel
.vercel/

# misc
*.tsbuildinfo
.turbo/

# local-only assets that shouldn't be committed
_reference/
demo website video.mp4
WhatsApp*
# Override: M4 source dir `lib/whatsapp/` is lowercased but still matches
# `WhatsApp*` on case-insensitive filesystems (Windows / macOS default).
!lib/whatsapp/
!lib/whatsapp/**
!lib/validators/whatsapp.ts
# …and any other lowercased `whatsapp*` SOURCE file anywhere under lib/ (e.g.
# lib/goals/whatsapp-dispatch.ts) — else ship.sh's `git add -A` silently skips
# it and prod fails to resolve the module at build time.
!lib/**/whatsapp*
# …and under components/. `components/ecos/whatsapp-panel.tsx` was imported by
# app/(app)/communications/[id]/page.tsx on 2026-09-10 but never committed,
# because this very rule skipped it — the production build then died with
# "Module not found". Exactly the failure the note above predicted, one
# directory over.
!components/**/whatsapp*
!app/api/whatsapp/
!app/api/whatsapp/**
!tests/unit/whatsapp-*.test.ts
ddd.py
*.jpeg
# …but letter signature assets under public/signatures/ MUST ship (else ship.sh's
# `git add -A` skips them and the PDF/letter render 404s the signature image).
!public/signatures/*.jpeg
vpinnacle.html
vpinnacle_dashboard*.html
credentials.md

